# stacks/gcp-identity — scaffold-time broad roles.
#
# The terraform-ci service account is granted roles/owner (mirror of the
# AWS AdministratorAccess attachment on the Terraform-CI role in
# stacks/identity). The Crossplane service account is granted roles/editor
# as a stand-in until stacks/crossplane produces a scoped custom role for
# GCP (same shape as the scoped IAM policy on the AWS side).
#
# Each binding has a TODO comment in stacks/gcp-identity/main.tf; tighten
# once each stack's real API surface is pinned.
AVD-GCP-0007
AVD-GCP-0011
AVD-GCP-0012

# The step-ca X.509 pool provider has no attribute_condition because
# allowed subject CNs are pinned per-service-account via the
# `principal://.../subject/<cn>` member on the impersonation binding.
# The per-SA pin is strictly tighter than a pool-level condition.
AVD-GCP-0068
